                <pb facs="0112" n="40" sameAs="frus:frus1909/pg40"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 836/123.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Brazilian Ambassador to
                        the Secretary of State.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Brazilian Embassy</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1909-01-22"><hi rendition="#italic">January 22,
                        1909</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Mr. Secretary of State</hi>: I have the honor to
                    bring to your knowledge that, according to a communication just received from
                    the Brazilian Government, by a decree No. 7283, of the 14th of January instant,
                    the ministry of finance renewed for the present fiscal year the reduction of 20
                    per cent previously granted to the American flour and to other articles imported
                    in Brazil from the United States of America.</p>
                <p>I avail, etc,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Joaquim Nabuco.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
